      chk_nf:"Notify me even when the browser is closed", nt_nf:"The notification shows only how many letters have arrived. Nobody can tell who sent them or what they say until the seal is opened (until you open Handpost).", nf_more:"Details", nf_d1:"Notifications travel through the push services run by Apple, Google and others. Some apps put the sender or the text into that channel, and then the companies along the way may be able to see it.", nf_d2:"The signal Handpost sends carries only the number of letters waiting in your mailbox, encrypted so that only your browser can read it. It carries neither the sender nor the text.", nf_d3:"Letters are sealed to a key that only your device holds (a quantum-resistant scheme). Neither the mailbox nor the companies along the way can open them. The part that shows the notification cannot use that key either, so it cannot show a name or any text.", nf_d4:"The channel still learns that \"something arrived for this device at this time\". The mailbox learns only whether a letter should ring (read receipts and the like do not ring). If that bothers you, turn the switch off.", nf_d5:"While Handpost is closed, each device is notified at most once a minute. There is no notification while you are looking at Handpost.", nf_working:"Checking…", nf_on:"Notifications are on.", nf_off:"Notifications are off.", nf_e_noid:"Create an account first.", nf_e_nosup:"This browser cannot notify you while it is closed.", nf_e_ios:"On iPhone and iPad this works only in Handpost added to the Home Screen (Share → Add to Home Screen). The Home Screen app has its own storage, separate from Safari, so set up your account there and then turn this switch on.", nf_e_nobox:"Notifications work once you have leased a mailbox.", nf_e_off:"Not connected to the mailbox. Try again once it is connected.", nf_e_denied:"Notifications for Handpost are blocked on this device. Allow them in the browser (or device) settings, then press again.", nf_e_old:"Your current mailbox was leased before notifications existed, so it does not support them. Move to a new mailbox to use them (Mailbox tab).", nf_e_fail:"Could not turn notifications on. See the log.",
    tip_bell:"Notifications on / off (slashed = no sound, no notification)", bl_card_n:"Letters waiting: {n}", bl_card_1:"A letter has arrived", bl_t_on:"Notifications on", bl_t_off:"Notifications off (no sound, no notification. Letters still arrive as before)",
    bl_t_open:"Notifications on (only while Handpost is open)\nNot set up for when it is closed: {why}", bl_t_snd:"Notifications on (sound only)\n{why}", bl_e_ask:"Notifications are not allowed on this device yet.",
